    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0715" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-26T20:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 26, 6.39 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I am positive Semenoff and Kalmarkoff<anchor n="35" xml:id="d589-f1"/> intend to
                    take possession Chinese Eastern by force and with the many Japanese soldiers now
                    on ground could do so as improbable Chinese would fight. This action would be
                    fatal blow to all our good offices. There is some reason to believe that Chinese
                    Government may be asked to appoint Semenoff director of Chinese Eastern, [which]
                    ought not to be permitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d589-f1" n="35" xml:id="d589-f1-content">
                <p>Undoubtedly Kalmykov, Ataman of the Ussuri Cossacks.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
